{
    "background_story": "Papi was a young soldier who served in a war-torn country. During a routine patrol, his unit was ambushed, and a grenade exploded nearby, sending shrapnel flying in all directions. Papi was hit, but his quick thinking and training allowed him to administer first aid to himself and his comrades. Despite his own injuries, he helped evacuate the wounded and provided cover fire until reinforcements arrived. The shrapnel had left Papi with a permanent scar above his left eyebrow, but it also earned him a reputation as a hero among his peers. After being honorably discharged, Papi returned home to a hero's welcome, but the memories of that fateful day stayed with him, a reminder of the sacrifices he made for his country and his fellow soldiers.",
